# The command the orchestrator test gate runs before an implementer subagent hands its work back: the first line that
# is not a comment, run with `bash -c` in the implementer's worktree, a non-zero exit blocks the handback.
# It is the Stop hook's script in its branch mode: the checks of everything the branch changed since its merge base with
# main (committed, uncommitted and new files), each only when the changes touch what it reads, in the checkout it is
# started in. The Swift checks go through tools/apple/check.sh, so the Xcode from .xcode-version is used, not the one
# xcode-select points at. A branch that changes nothing a check reads (documents only) passes with nothing run.
.claude/hooks/stop-checks.sh --branch main
